{
  "id": "cr",
  "term": "CR",
  "definition": "CR stands for cognitive reserve: the accumulated cognitive and brain resources built across the lifespan that can help explain why people with similar brain pathology show different levels of thinking ability. It is often inferred from life experiences such as education, complex work, and mentally stimulating activities, and its protective value may change across healthy aging and dementia stages.",
